---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
const nativeTargets = [
  ["window-animation", "duration, enterOffset, focusOpacity, exitScale, easing", "A complete animation profile; turning animations off in Settings still wins."],
  ["shell-animation", "{ duration }", "One duration from 0 to 600 ms for shell transitions."],
  ["window-rules", "{ workspace, maximized }", "The rule for a new ordinary window; the workspace must exist."],
  ["window-layout", "{ windows:[{id,x,y,width,height},...] }", "Every non-minimized id once, positive sizes, inside the work area; overlap only when the template allows it."],
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Plugins that run in the compositor." section="plugins" summary="Native effect plugins change how LunaDash animates, places and lays out windows. Create one with the generator, build it with the CMake SDK and enable it through the control API.">
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#model">Model</a><a href="#create">Create</a><a href="#manifest">Manifest</a><a href="#targets">Targets</a><a href="#native">Contract</a><a href="#settings">Settings</a><a href="#enable">Install and enable</a><a href="#debug">Debug</a></nav>

  <h2 id="model">What a plugin is</h2>
  <p>A plugin is an <code>effect</code>: a shared library loaded into the compositor. For its target feature LunaDash sends a JSON request with the built-in result, and the plugin answers with a complete replacement (<code>replace</code>) or an adjusted result (<code>augment</code>). Each target accepts one enabled plugin. The shell's look is changed in the <a href="../shell/">shell itself</a>, not through plugins.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Plugins are trusted native code.</strong> Metadata and ABI checks are compatibility checks, not signing or a sandbox; a crash or hang takes down the compositor. Plugins stay disabled until you enable them.</p></div>

  <h2 id="create">Create, build and install</h2>
  <CodeBlock label="GENERATOR" code={'lunadash-create-plugin --list\nlunadash-create-plugin --target window-layout --id org.example.layout --output my-layout'} />
  <p>Ids match <code>^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]+$</code>; the generator needs a new output directory.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="CMAKELISTS.TXT" code={'cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.21)\nproject(MyLunaDashPlugin LANGUAGES C CXX)\nfind_package(LunaDashPlugin 2 CONFIG REQUIRED)\nlunadash_add_plugin(my_plugin\n  METADATA "metadata.json"\n  SOURCES Effect.cpp\n)'} />
  <CodeBlock label="ONE-USER INSTALL" code={'cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local"\ncmake --build build\ncmake --install build'} />

  <h2 id="manifest">metadata.json</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={'{\n "schemaVersion":2,\n "sdk":{"name":"LunaDash","apiVersion":2},\n "id":"org.example.layout","name":"Example layout","version":"1.0.0",\n "author":{"name":"Your name"},\n "type":"effect","target":"window-layout","mode":"replace","entry":"libmy_plugin.so",\n "enabledByDefault":false,\n "settings":{"gap":{"type":"integer","default":12,"control":"slider","minimum":0,"maximum":64}}\n}'} />
  <p>A package can declare up to 16 implementations in <code>targets</code>, sharing one <code>.so</code>. <code>"windowTemplate":"stacking"</code> on a <code>window-layout</code> replacement selects the overlapping, freely movable window policy.</p>

  <h2 id="targets">Targets</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Target</th><th>Response</th><th>Validation</th></tr></thead><tbody>{nativeTargets.map(([target, response, validation]) => <tr><td class="api-method">{target}</td><td><code>{response}</code></td><td>{validation}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>

  <h2 id="native">The contract</h2>
  <p>The SDK generates the exported <code>ludash_plugin_entry_v2</code>; you implement <code>ludash_plugin_process(request, response, capacity)</code> and return the UTF-8 JSON length (without the NUL) or a negative value. Hooks run on the compositor thread: never block, keep host pointers or start work that outlives the call.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="WINDOW-LAYOUT REQUEST" code={'{\n "target":"window-layout","mode":"replace",\n "context":{"workspace":0,"area":{"x":0,"y":40,"width":1920,"height":1040},"newWindows":[23],"windowTemplate":"tiling","allowOverlap":false},\n "builtin":{"windows":[...]},"current":{},"settings":{"gap":12}\n}'} />
  <p><code>builtin</code> is always present; <code>augment</code> also receives the previous valid result in <code>current</code>. Return a complete object. Invalid output keeps the previous valid result and quarantines the plugin.</p>

  <h2 id="settings">Plugin settings</h2>
  <p>Settings use toggle (boolean), select (enum), number and slider (bounded) controls; every field needs a type and a default.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={'"settings":{\n "glow":{"type":"boolean","default":true,"control":"toggle"},\n "quality":{"type":"string","default":"medium","control":"select","enum":["low","medium","high"]},\n "strength":{"type":"number","default":0.5,"control":"slider","minimum":0,"maximum":1}\n}'} />

  <h2 id="enable">Install and enable</h2>
  <p>An SDK-built package is found under <code>lunadash/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code> in the XDG data directories, normally <code>~/.local/share/lunadash/plugins/&lt;id&gt;</code>; the SDK's <code>.lunadash-sdk.json</code> receipt must match the metadata. Enable it in <code>~/.config/LuDash/extensions.json</code> through the control API:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={'lunadashctl extension-save \'{"schemaVersion":1,"builtins":{},"plugins":{"org.example.layout":{"enabled":true,"mode":"replace","settings":{"gap":16}}}}\''} />
  <p>Disable a plugin before replacing its library, install the new build, then enable it again.</p>

  <h2 id="debug">Debug checklist</h2>
  <ol><li>Check the target with <code>lunadash-create-plugin --list</code>.</li><li>Rebuild with LunaDashPlugin 2 after editing the metadata.</li><li>Read <code>lunadashctl status</code> → <code>extensions.installed</code> for the status, error and settings.</li><li>After fixing, clear the error with an empty <code>extension-error</code> request.</li></ol>
</DocsLayout>
